The generated threat intelligence module takes the Suricata log generated in B23, and parses every alert, enriching each one with threat context from a local knowledge 
base, correlates related alerts into attack patterns, extracts IOCs, and produces a structured threat intelligence report.
The python file was generated by Claude.
First, it defines a local threat intelligence knowledge base that maps signature IDs to attack tactics, techniques, severity levels and MITRE ATT&CK descriptions, and
recommended responses. A Suricata log is fed into the program, where important information is extracted from each alert. This includes, timestamps, signature IDs, source
and destination IP addresses, port numbers and protocols. If the signature IDs match one stored in the local knowledge base, that log entry is 'enriched', where the entry
is given more detailed context. The attacks are grouped by source IP and signatures, to identify suspicious behaviours. If a single IP causes multiple attacks, they are labelled
as "Multi-stage Activity", and if the same signature causes multiple alerts, it is classified as a "Sustained Attack". 
